2. ALTERNATIVE PATH 1: U.S. Diplomatic Freeze + Soviet 
Private Diplomacy
Logic:• State Department's preference aligns with Soviet willingness for secret 
negotiations
• Both sides' constraint to avoid nuclear war drives diplomatic solution
• Minimizes immediate escalation while addressing both sides' goals
• Variable impacts: Tension remains moderate, Diplomatic Support increases
3. ALTERNATIVE PATH 2: U.S. Air Strikes + Soviet 
Defensive Alert
Logic:• Defense Department pressure + time constraints push U.S. to military 
option
• Soviet military response per their "direct_attack" trigger threshold
• Represents high-risk scenario both sides' militaries are prepared for
• Variable impacts: Tension +0.75, high risk of triggering "Military Conflict 
Risk Increased"
